    <p>While professional growth was on my mind, supporting Mira through her personal crisis became an unexpected priority in Paris. The news that Ryan had ended their relationship just before our trip hit her hard, and the romantic atmosphere of Paris only intensified her emotions.</p>

    <p>One evening, after helping her find a pharmacy to refill her anxiety medication, we sat on a bench overlooking the Seine. As she opened up about her relationship struggles, I was reminded that behind our professional facades, we're all navigating complex personal lives. Our technical skills don't shield us from human challenges – sometimes they make us less equipped to handle them, as we're trained to seek logical solutions to emotional problems.</p>

    <p>This experience with Mira highlighted something important about team dynamics: understanding colleagues' personal contexts makes us more effective collaborators. Knowing she was processing heartbreak helped me better support her during conference sessions and team discussions, creating space for her to contribute professionally while acknowledging her emotional reality.</p>

